by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-12T14:04:56Z

Reopening this: it was closed for inactivity, not rejected. I compared it with #63845, which proposed an `#[AsFactory]` attribute on the factory side, and I prefer this shape, so I closed that one in favour of this. Putting `factory` next to `constructor` on the existing attribute means no new attribute, no new compiler pass, the whole factory syntax including expressions, and the attribute stays on the class being built, so it never has to register a service that was not declared.

I rebased onto 8.2 and pushed. What changed:

 * XML config support was removed from the component in the meantime (af1f0305c6b), so the XSD change, `XmlFileLoaderTest` and the XML fixture are gone.
 * The keyword lists moved to `ContentLoaderTrait`, so `'factory'` was added to `INSTANCEOF_KEYWORDS` there.
 * `factory` is now also declared under `_instanceof` in `services.schema.json` and in the `InstanceofType` shape of `AppReference`, which are what the array-shape PHP config format is checked against. The generated `reference.php` fixture follows.
 * The `instanceof_factory.php` fixture is written with the array shape rather than the fluent PHP-DSL, and the `InstanceofConfigurator::factory()` change is dropped: the DSL is on its way out, so it is not worth extending.
 * The CHANGELOG entry moved from 7.4 to 8.2, and the two lines are merged into one.
 * `$factory` goes last in the constructor, after `$resourceTags` which landed since.
 * `testServiceWithSameNameAsInterfaceAndFactoryIsNotTagged()` keeps `#[IgnoreDeprecations]` and `#[Group('legacy')]` alongside your data provider: both fixtures use `!tagged_iterator`, which is what those markers are for.
 * `AutoconfigureWithStaticSelfFactory::create()` returns `new static()` rather than `new self()`, since it is declared `: static`.

The DependencyInjection suite is green (1807 tests), as are FrameworkBundle's and Routing's. I also checked that an explicit `factory` on a definition still wins over one coming from `_instanceof`.

Rebased again now that #65290 is merged up, so the `reference.php` fixture is untouched here: it tolerates the shape difference on its own, which matters because FrameworkBundle's low-deps and high-deps jobs install `symfony/dependency-injection` from packagist and generate the file from a released `AppReference`. I also checked that an explicit `factory` on a definition still wins over one coming from `_instanceof`.

On @zolex's suggestion to deprecate `constructor` in favour of `factory`: not in this PR. `constructor` and `factory` already coexist in the config formats, so this only brings the attribute in line with them rather than adding new overlap. Worth a separate discussion.

Thanks for the work, and for coming back to it after so long a wait.
